        "subject": "LU-21043 tests: wait for precreated objects in sanity/51d",
        "message": "LU-21043 tests: wait for precreated objects in sanity/51d\n\nsanity test_51d raised osp.*.create_count on all MDTs, then slept a\nfixed 8 seconds before each pass of test_51d_sub.  With many MDTs\n(12 MDTs, 8 OSTs) every OST had to precreate create_count objects for\neach MDT, and after 8 seconds many OSPs still had only the initial\nobjects.  LOD round-robin would skip the OSTs whose pool was empty,\nand the test would fail with too few objects on some OSTs and too\nmany first stripes on the next OST.\n\nSet create_count only on the MDTs that hold the stripes of $tdir,\nsince all of the files are created there, and restore it with\nstack_trap.  Add sub_51d_wait_precreate() to replace the sleep.  It\nwaits until each OSP of those MDTs, highest index first, has enough\nobjects precreated for one pass (prealloc_last_id - prealloc_next_id\n+ 1), and fails the test if precreation does not catch up.  It waits\nin 10s slices and sets create_count again between them if the OSP\nlowered it for a slow OST.\n\nWhen prealloc_last_id of an OSP reaches the end of its FID sequence\n(seq.cli-*OST*-super.width, 16384 objects with OSTSEQWIDTH=0x20000\nand 8 OSTs), the OSP sends no more precreates until its pool is used\nup and osp_precreate_rollover_new_seq() moves it to a new sequence,\nso the pool would never refill while the test waits.  Add\nsub_51d_use_seq_end(), called between slices, to create and unlink\n1-stripe files on each such OST in $tdir.fill.<mdtidx> on that MDT,\nusing up the objects left so the OSP moves to the next sequence and\nrefills.  These files are outside $tdir, so test_51d_sub does not\ncount them.  Count a pool used up to the end of its sequence as\nempty, since prealloc_next_id shows 1 until the OSP rolls over.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=51d,ONLY_REPEAT=20 mdscount=2 mdtcount=12 ostcount=8\nFixes: cf35c54224b3 (\"LU-14745 tests: ensure sanity/51d has enough objects\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I90183deaf368081d18c70a55329f9818db3ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70064\nReviewed-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
